msgstr ""

#: ../../source/reference/configuration/options.md
msgid "`-f EURIZON-EN23`"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/reference/configuration/options.md:91
msgid ""
"The **configured** format, and the strongest of the three sources a job "
"takes its format from. Left unset, the job detects the format from its "
"documents: first from the repository's document classification, which "
"reads their first pages, then from `url_mapping.csv`, which reads their "
"URLs — so a local file can be recognised too, as long as the repository "
"has rules for it. The job runs only with a complete format; a partial "
"one, or none at all, fails that job alone."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/reference/configuration/options.md:97
msgid ""
"Set, it is the format the job runs, but the document classification still"
" runs and the URL is still looked up: a source that **disagrees** with "
"the configured format is a `WARN`, which no setting switches off, and the"
" configured format is used. A misspelt format is reported when the job "
"loads its recipe, after its documents have been resolved."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/reference/configuration/options.md:102
#, python-brace-format
msgid ""
"The full order of the sources, how they combine, and every crossing with "
"its log level are in {doc}`../cli/freeports` (\"Where the format comes "
"from\")."
msgstr ""

